---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Terms of use — AirScanner"
  description="Plain-English terms for using AirScanner and this website, including scanner requirements, checking output, and your consumer rights."
  legal
>
  <header class="page-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">AirScanner / Terms</p>
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="legal-date">Effective <time datetime="2026-09-28">28 September 2026</time></p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      These terms cover your use of the AirScanner app and this informational
      website. AirScanner connects an iPhone or iPad to a compatible flatbed
      scanner, saves PDFs, and recognizes text on-device for in-app search.
      Our <a href={`${base}privacy/`}>privacy policy</a> explains data handling.
    </p>

    <h2>Use it with permission</h2>
    <p>
      Scan only documents you own or are authorized to scan, and connect only to
      scanners and networks you are allowed to use. Respect applicable law and
      other people’s privacy and intellectual property rights. You retain your
      rights in your documents; these terms do not transfer them to the developer.
    </p>

    <h2>What you need</h2>
    <p>
      AirScanner requires iOS or iPadOS 17 or later and a real
      eSCL/AirScan-compatible flatbed scanner on the same local Wi-Fi network.
      It is not a camera scanner, and AirPrint support alone does not establish
      compatibility. Local Network permission is required. Isolated guest networks
      can prevent connections; keep the app open while scanning.
    </p>
    <p>
      Available scan settings and results depend on your scanner, its firmware,
      your network, and your operating system. Compatibility with every scanner,
      network setup, or future system version is not guaranteed. Use trusted
      networks: scanner transport may be unencrypted, as explained in the privacy
      policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Check your output and keep backups</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Review saved PDFs for completeness, legibility, and correct page content
        before relying on them or discarding originals. Scans capture the full
        platen; automatic cropping is not provided.
      </li>
      <li>
        Check recognized text before using or sharing it. OCR can miss or misread
        text, and exported PDFs do not receive a searchable OCR text layer.
      </li>
      <li>
        Treat empty-glass checks as an estimate, not proof that the glass is empty
        or a document has been detected correctly.
      </li>
      <li>
        Keep backups of important documents. Local app storage is not an archive
        or a backup service; deletion, device loss, or system changes can affect
        access to your files.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other services you choose</h2>
    <p>
      Exports, sharing, Photos, clipboard features, and backups depend on the apps
      and system services you use. Optional ratings are handled by Apple. This
      website is hosted by GitHub Pages, and public support issues are handled by
      GitHub. Those providers’ terms and privacy policies apply to their services;
      AirScanner does not control their availability or handling of copies you
      send to them.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability and responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, the app and website are provided “as is” and
      “as available,” without additional warranties. The developer does not
      guarantee uninterrupted or error-free operation, scanner compatibility,
      accurate OCR, successful scans, or suitability for a particular purpose.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, the developer is not liable for losses that
      were not reasonably foreseeable from use of the app or website. This does
      not exclude or limit liability where doing so would be unlawful, including
      liability for fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence
      where protected by applicable law.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your mandatory consumer rights remain intact.</strong> Nothing here
      excludes statutory guarantees, remedies, or other rights that cannot legally
      be excluded or limited. Those protections take priority over these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      Revised terms will be published here with a new effective date and apply
      prospectively, not to earlier use. Changes cannot remove rights you already
      have under applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>General questions</h2>
    <p>
      Use the <a href="https://github.com/jtvargas/airscanner-web/issues">public website-repository issues</a>
      for general questions about the app, website, or these terms. This is a public
      channel, not a confidential support service, and no response time is promised.
      <strong>Do not include documents, personal information, or network identifiers</strong>
      such as IP addresses, Wi-Fi names, or scanner serial numbers.
    </p>
    <p><a href={`${base}privacy/`}>Read the privacy policy</a> or <a href={base}>return to AirScanner</a>.</p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
